# Allowlist rather than denylist.
#
# Everything is excluded first and only what the build genuinely needs is added
# back. A denylist would eventually leak something: this repository is worked on
# beside real credential files (credentials.json, service-account keys, token.json)
# and generated reports full of personal data, and any of those landing in the
# build context would end up readable in the image history.
*

# Module graph.
!go.mod
!go.sum

# Application source. Test files are matched by the directory rules but are not
# compiled into the binary.
!cmd/
!internal/

# The example configuration, shipped as documentation inside the image.
!conf/xls_report.ini

# Re-exclude anything sensitive or bulky that the rules above might have pulled in.
**/*_test.go
**/testdata/
**/*.xlsx
**/*.xls
**/*.log
**/token.json
**/credentials.json
**/client_secret*.json
**/service-account*.json
**/*.pem
**/*.p12
